{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "We have two completed experiments: config_015 (multimodal, pca_n2000+resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc and config_023 (image_only, resnet50, avgpool) at 0.328 acc. The ~29-point gap shows RNA adds substantial value, but we cannot yet decompose how much signal comes from RNA alone versus a synergistic interaction. config_013 (rna_only, pca_n2000, avgpool, multiprofile) completes the three-way modality decomposition (image_only vs RNA_only vs multimodal) while holding the RNA encoder, aggregation, and profile setting identical to config_015. If RNA-only approaches ~0.50, the image contribution is modest and future effort should target RNA encoder or fusion; if RNA-only is near image-only (~0.33), the gain is strongly synergistic and fusion/aggregation design becomes the priority. This single experiment resolves the largest remaining uncertainty about where to invest limited budget, making it more informative than testing a new encoder or fusion variant before we know which modality is the primary driver."
}

